	"changelog": "\n2026.08.18: Updated the bundled yt-dlp library (2026.07.04 to a 2026.08.17 pre-release build) to fix YouTube extraction breaking for pasted links (\"Could not fetch data\") - YouTube had changed something extraction-dependent since the previous release, and yt-dlp's maintainers had already shipped several fix builds ahead of their next stable release. Currently-live broadcasts now open directly in the user's default browser instead of playing inside the add-on, since the browser's own native YouTube player handles live playback more reliably than the bundled offline media player ever could. Added a \"Live\" search type alongside Video/Playlist/Channel, to find currently-live broadcasts by keyword directly from the Search and Download tab (previously only reachable per-channel via the Subscriptions tab's Live section). Also fixes an unrelated ordinary-video playback bug where mpv's own internal link resolver was incorrectly re-engaging on links this add-on had already resolved itself, occasionally cutting playback short before the end.\n2026.07.19: Full-featured release. Search, play, and download YouTube videos, playlists, and channels entirely by keyboard - audio playback with full transport control (play/pause, seek, volume, speed, previous/next with automatic continue), a sleep timer, personal playlist management, and a Subscriptions tab that browses a followed channel's Videos, Shorts, Live, and Playlists the way YouTube itself organizes them. Download to MP3 or MP4 with selectable quality, auto-sorted into folders by playlist or channel name. Full English/Thai interface with instant switching (Control+T).\n",
